From: Armada <noreply@armada>
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: allow linear composition output

The Retroid Pocket Duo's bottom panel corrupts UBWC scanout, while the same
mode with a linear composition buffer is clean. Allow a compositor instance
to opt into the existing linear-buffer allocation path. Imported client
images are unchanged. Pair this with --force-composition to prevent direct
scanout from bypassing the output buffer.

This is a workaround until the shared-buffer UBWC issue is resolved.
---
diff --git a/src/rendervulkan.cpp b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
--- a/src/rendervulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
@@ -3291,6 +3291,7 @@ static bool vulkan_make_output_images( VulkanOutput_t *pOutput )
 	outputImageflags.bStorage = true;
 	outputImageflags.bTransferSrc = true; // for screenshots
 	outputImageflags.bSampled = true; // for pipewire blits
+	outputImageflags.bLinear = env_to_bool( getenv( "GAMESCOPE_FORCE_LINEAR_OUTPUT" ) );
 	outputImageflags.bOutputImage = true;
 
 	pOutput->outputImages.resize(3); // extra image for partial composition.
